<%# The poll holds off while a tap is out. #669.

    A tap's answer is the panel it changed and the rest cue that starts the next rest, and
    htmx swaps the panel into the element that sent the tap. A poll that comes back first
    replaces every panel -- the tapping form with them -- and htmx, finding the sender gone
    from the page, throws the tap's whole answer away. The rows look right, because the poll
    drew the same ones, and the rest timer never hears that a set was finished: it goes on
    counting the last set's rest. That is what "tapping RPE doesn't reset the timer" was.

    It is not a rare overlap. The tap's own write rings the session stream (#592), the stream
    fires the poll, and that poll still asks about the fingerprint the page loaded with --
    the tap's answer is the thing that brings the new one -- so it finds a change and sends
    every panel back, racing the answer it was caused by.

    So while any set tap is out, a poll is not sent, and one already sent is not swapped. It
    loses nothing: the tap's answer re-arms the poller with what the tap made true (#249),
    and the fifteen-second poll and the next doorbell carry on from there. A poll is only
    ever a catch-up, and nothing is behind while the screen is waiting on its own tap.

    Counted, not flagged, because two taps can be out at once -- a superset ticked off in
    one motion. And released on the request's own loadend rather than on htmx:afterRequest:
    that event is fired on the form that sent the tap, and a form swapped out of the page
    fires it into nothing, which would leave the count up and the poll held for good. loadend
    fires on the request whatever has happened to the page, for an answer, an error, a
    timeout or an abort alike.

    Outside #session-body with the stream and the banner, for their reason: everything in
    there is replaced on every swap, and this has to outlive the swaps it is about. %>
<script>
  (function () {
    var out = 0;

    function isTap(event) {
      var config = event.detail && event.detail.requestConfig;
      return !!(config && config.path && /\/sets\/\d+\/complete$/.test(config.path));
    }

    function isPoll(event) {
      var config = event.detail && event.detail.requestConfig;
      return !!(config && config.path && config.path.indexOf('/session/changes') !== -1);
    }

    document.body.addEventListener('htmx:beforeRequest', function (event) {
      if (isPoll(event) && out > 0) { event.preventDefault(); return; }
      if (!isTap(event) || !event.detail.xhr) { return; }
      out += 1;
      event.detail.xhr.addEventListener('loadend', function () { out = Math.max(0, out - 1); });
    });

    document.body.addEventListener('htmx:beforeSwap', function (event) {
      if (isPoll(event) && out > 0) { event.detail.shouldSwap = false; }
    });
  })();
</script>
